Answer parts (a), (b) and (c) below. Give each value in its simplest form.', '{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Question 1 — 6 marks"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "mathInline", "attrs": {"latex": "256 = 4^a"}}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "mathInline", "attrs": {"latex": "\\frac{3}{8} \\times \\frac{32}{9} = 2^b \\times 3^c"}}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "mathInline", "attrs": {"latex": "\\sqrt{45} - d\\sqrt{e} = \\sqrt{5}"}}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Answer parts (a), (b) and (c) below. Give each value in its simplest form."}]}]}'::jsonb, '$4^4 = 256$ so $a = 4$. $\frac{3}{8}\times\frac{32}{9} = \frac{4}{3} = 2^2 3^{-1}$, so $b = 2$ and $c = -1$. $\sqrt{45} = 3\sqrt{5}$, so $3\sqrt5 - d\sqrt e = \sqrt5$ gives $d\sqrt e = 2\sqrt5$, hence $d = 2$ and $e = 5$.',
        6, 'medium', 'Number', 'indices, fractions and surds',
        array['MYP 5', 'Mathematics', 'IB eAssessment', 'Standard', 'May 2025', 'ib-myp5-mathematics-standard-may-2025']::text[],
