by term.", "The surd part must match, so e is the number under the root in 2√5."]}], "marks_status": "verified", "marks_note": "Total 6 marks printed by the paper: (a) 1, (b) 2, (c) 3. The split of (b) into b and c, and of (c) into the simplified surd, d and e, is a subdivision of those printed totals."}'::jsonb,
