One side of the rectangle is $5x$ and its area is $140$ units².', '{"type": "doc", "content": [{"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Question 5 — 8 marks"}]}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The following diagram shows a rectangle."}]}, {"type": "graphBlock", "attrs": {"spec": {"version": 1, "title": "Rectangle — diagram not to scale", "domain": {"xMin": 0, "xMax": 10, "yMin": 0, "yMax": 6, "gridStep": null, "showGrid": true, "showAxes": true, "showCoordinates": false, "showLegend": false, "showIntersections": false, "equalScale": false}, "functions": [], "points": [], "segments": [{"id": "top", "x1": 1, "y1": 4.5, "x2": 8.4, "y2": 4.5, "color": "#0a5c36", "style": "solid", "width": 2, "label": "", "visible": true}, {"id": "right", "x1": 8.4, "y1": 4.5, "x2": 8.4, "y2": 1.5, "color": "#0a5c36", "style": "solid", "width": 2, "label": "", "visible": true}, {"id": "bottom", "x1": 1, "y1": 1.5, "x2": 8.4, "y2": 1.5, "color": "#0a5c36", "style": "solid", "width": 2, "label": "", "visible": true}, {"id": "left", "x1": 1, "y1": 1.5, "x2": 1, "y2": 4.5, "color": "#0a5c36", "style": "solid", "width": 2, "label": "", "visible": true}], "annotations": [{"id": "len", "x": 4.4, "y": 5.15, "text": "5x", "color": "#333333"}, {"id": "area", "x": 4.0, "y": 2.7, "text": "Area = 140 units²", "color": "#333333"}], "strokes": [], "regions": [], "xLabel": "x", "yLabel": "y"}}}, {"type": "paragraph", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "One side of the rectangle is $5x$ and its area is $140$ units²."}]}]}'::jsonb, '$5x^2 = 140$ so $x = \sqrt{28} = 2\sqrt7 \approx 5.29$. Length $= 5x \approx 26.46$ units, width $\approx 5.29$ units. Enlarged area 1260 = 9 × 140, so the linear scale factor is 3: length ≈ 79.37 units, width ≈ 15.87 units.',
        8, 'medium', 'Algebra', 'quadratic models and enlargement',
        array['MYP 5', 'Mathematics', 'IB eAssessment', 'Standard', 'May 2025', 'ib-myp5-mathematics-standard-may-2025']::text[],
        'published', '{"question_number": "Question 5", "paper_question": 5, "part_label": "Question 5", "marks": 8, "calculator": true, "calculator_policy": "on_screen_only", "assessment_style": "ib_myp_eassessment", "source": "ib-myp5-mathematics-standard-may-2025", "parts": [{"id": "a", "label": "(a)", "kind": "expression", "points": 4, "prompt": "Find the value of x.", "accepted": ["\\sqrt{28}", "sqrt28", "2\\sqrt{7}", "2sqrt7", "\\sqrt{28}\\text{ units}", "5.29", "5.3", "5.292"], "placeholder": "x =", "hints": ["The area of a rectangle is length × width. Write an equation in x.", "Area = 5x × x = 5x² = 140, so x² = 28."]}, {"id": "b", "label": "(b) length", "kind": "numeric", "points": 0.5, "prompt": "Length of the rectangle", "answer": 26.46, "tolerance": 0.1, "unit": "units", "placeholder": "length", "hints": ["The length is the side printed as 5x.", "Substitute your x into 5x."]}, {"id": "b2", "label": "(b) width", "kind": "numeric", "points": 0.5, "prompt": "Width of the rectangle", "answer": 5.29, "tolerance": 0.1, "unit": "units", "placeholder": "width", "hints": ["The width is the remaining side, which is x.", "Use your value of x directly."]}, {"id": "c", "label": "(c) enlarged length", "kind": "numeric", "points": 1.5, "prompt": "The rectangle is enlarged. The area of the enlarged rectangle is 1260 units². Find the length of the enlarged rectangle.", "answer": 79.37, "tolerance": 0.2, "unit": "units", "placeholder": "length", "hints": ["Compare the areas: 1260 ÷ 140 = 9. What is the linear scale factor?", "A scale factor of 3 for length gives 9 for area, so multiply the length by 3."]}, {"id": "c2", "label": "(c) enlarged width", "kind": "numeric", "points": 1.5, "prompt": "Find the width of the enlarged rectangle.", "answer": 15.87, "tolerance": 0.2, "unit": "units", "placeholder": "width", "hints": ["Use the same linear scale factor you found for the length.", "Multiply the original width by 3."]}], "marks_status": "verified", "marks_note": "Total 8 marks printed by the paper: (a) 4, (b) 1, (c) 3. (b) and (c) are split across their two values, each summing to the printed total. The width of the rectangle is inferred to be x: the paper prints only the side 5x and the area, and part (b) asks for both length and width after finding x."}'::jsonb,
