values ('d1500000-0000-4000-8000-000000001008', '0a400000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'open_ended', 'Question 6(a) — 3 marks
In this question you will make calculations for tidal energy.
Renewable energy technology has advanced by making use of changing coastal tides to provide clean and reliable energy. There are some physical requirements needed in order to utilise energy from tides. It is essential to have a large tidal range. The tidal range is the difference in height of the low tide and the high tide. Another physical requirement is a suitable location to create a large tidal lagoon. A tidal lagoon is a lake that holds water at high tide. For financial and ecological reasons, the best location for a tidal lagoon is where the coastline forms a bay. Tidal energy is dependent on the tidal range and the area of the lagoon seabed.
The following diagram shows an isosceles triangle with dimensions indicated on the diagram.

[Figure: Design T — diagram not to scale]
